<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="china_geostrategic_push::ai_capability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in attacks on commercial shipping prompts Chinese state and corporate actors to accelerate procurement and development of AI systems for maritime domain awareness, autonomous vessels and logistics optimization to protect trade routes and reduce exposure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">china_geostrategic_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="european_institutional_f::sovereign_bond_spreads" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in attacks on commercial vessels produces immediate insurance and commodity‑price shocks and prompts short‑term investor flight from riskier euro‑area debt, widening sovereign spreads especially for fiscally fragile states.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">european_institutional_f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="global_oil_market_shock::product_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased attacks on tankers produce immediate cargo delays, higher insurance and freight costs and a trader risk-premium that is passed into spot and futures refined-fuel prices, pushing up regional product price levels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">More frequent/intense attacks cause cancellations and rerouting of diesel cargoes and off-spec deliveries, reducing delivered volumes to consuming markets and widening diesel shortfalls (a more negative supply gap).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in attacks on commercial shipping pushes up energy prices and political sensitivity to further energy-sector penalties, weakening domestic and coalition appetite to expand or tighten sanctions on Russia's energy exports.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
