<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" target="china_geostrategic_push::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An elevated regional military posture increases the likelihood of incidents and interstate alignments that draw in major powers, directly intensifying strategic friction and diplomatic hostility involving China and its competitors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">china_geostrategic_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" target="european_institutional_f::monetary_credibility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained escalation in regional military deployments raises political pressure on central banks to prioritize growth/support measures (energy subsidies, easing) over inflation targets, eroding market perceptions of consistent commitment to stated monetary rules.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">european_institutional_f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" target="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Augmented naval deployments and convoy protections reduce the success rate and frequency of opportunistic maritime attacks and interdictions, thereby lowering the short-term intensity and incidence of geopolitical incidents that disrupt energy logistics.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_force_projectio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained elevation of naval and military posture in the Gulf forces the U.S. and NATO to reassign ships, air assets and strategic lift to the region, directly reducing available units, pre-positioned stocks and deployment tempo for conventional operations related to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
