</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="china_geostrategic_push::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment and operational coordination among the US and its allies forged during the Russia–Ukraine war is redirected into coordinated strategic posture and deterrence in the Indo‑Pacific, increasing bilateral and multilateral tensions with China.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_geostrategic_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="european_institutional_f::monetary_credibility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained fall in alliance cohesion creates differentiated fiscal responses and political pressure on the ECB (calls for monetary financing or relaxed remit), weakening market belief in the central bank's independence and commitment to its stated inflation objectives.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">european_institutional_f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater cohesion and resource commitment among Western allies to counter Russia leads the United States and partners to redeploy naval and air assets toward Europe, reducing sustained forward deployments and deterrent posture in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
