  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" target="global_oil_market_shock::refining_profit_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" target="global_oil_market_shock::regulatory_scrutiny_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" target="european_institutional_f::gdp_growth_momentum" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A diesel shortfall immediately constrains freight, construction and agricultural logistics, causing production disruptions and inventory bottlenecks that slow industrial output and overall GDP momentum.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">european_institutional_f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" target="iran_gulf_standoff::supply_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in the diesel supply gap (i.e., supply exceeding demand) reduces market and stakeholder assessments of near‑term disruption risk, whereas a shrinking/negative gap raises perceived supply risk; hence movements in the gap directly alter risk perception.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::diesel_supply_gap" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_force_projectio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A larger diesel supply surplus (positive gap) improves fuel availability for Ukrainian and allied logistics and mechanized operations, degrading Russia's relative ability to expand cross‑border conventional operations; conversely a shortage would favor Russian operational freedom.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
