<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" target="china_geostrategic_push::export_control_restrict" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in geopolitical conflict intensity prompts governments to impose or tighten formal export controls and licensing on critical components and know‑how to deny adversaries capabilities and to reduce technology leakage.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_geostrategic_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" target="european_institutional_f::sovereign_bond_spreads" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising geopolitical conflict raises the perceived risk of energy‑supply shocks and fiscal stress for energy‑importing European states, prompting investors to demand higher sovereign risk premia and widen spreads.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">european_institutional_f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" target="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in geopolitical conflict intensity increases the propensity for state and proxy actors to conduct interdiction, harassment, mining, and missile/DRONE strikes on commercial vessels in the Gulf as part of broader coercive or asymmetric campaigns.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" target="iran_gulf_standoff::military_posture" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising conflict intensity prompts regional and extra‑regional powers to escalate naval deployments, readiness levels, and patrols in the maritime domain to protect shipping and deter adversaries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shock::geo_conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in geopolitical incidents that threaten energy flows (e.g., attacks on tankers or choke points) prompts allied governments to coordinate energy-security, military posture, and sanctions policy, increasing practical cohesion around the Russia-Ukraine response.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
