  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in EU sovereign spreads raises borrowing costs and forces short‑term fiscal reprioritization in member states, slowing or cutting planned defence aid and procurement deliveries to Ukraine and thereby reducing allied/Ukraine conventional force projection in contested areas.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
